    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `locality` field is a derived, read-only value returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Since the GET pipeline reloads the owner from the database and there's no `locality` column, deriving it purely from the persisted `city` at response-mapping time is the only clean approach \u2014 mirroring how the existing derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`) are computed in the `OwnerMapper`.\n\nThree edits:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`CityRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 A small closed-table lookup helper: `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD` (case-insensitive, trimmed), returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for anything else or a null city.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression deriving `locality` from `owner.getCity()` via `CityRegion.localityOf(...)`, alongside the existing derived-field mappings.\n\nThe two acceptance tests confirm both branches: `Sydney \u2192 \"NSW\"` and a random unmapped city \u2192 `\"UNKNOWN\"`.",
